    text: "Hoi An Old Town is the romantic heart: yellow walls, tailor shops, river reflections and lantern evenings. Staying inside or on the fringe means walking to cafés, assembly halls and night markets within minutes. The trade-off is crowds, higher rates in peak season and occasional street noise after dark. Boutique hotels and heritage conversions dominate the inventory.\n\nMorning light before tour groups arrive is magical; evenings glow with lanterns and river boats. Tailors, leather shops and lantern makers invite browsing, though quality varies—take time comparing. Tickets are required for many historic houses; keep them handy. If you need deep quiet sleep during festival peaks, consider a nearby quieter cluster for some nights.\n\nChoose Ancient Town if atmosphere is the priority and you are happy to immerse fully. Then step to An Bang or Cam Chau on other nights if you need quieter sleep after peak evenings. Few places in Vietnam deliver this much intimacy between lodging and cultural landscape. Practical notes help most visitors settle faster. Confirm check-in times, luggage storage and Grab pickup points with your hotel, especially if you arrive late or leave early for a flight or day trip. Weather and season change the feel of any neighbourhood. Heat, rain, festival crowds and school holidays can shift noise levels and prices, so build a little flexibility into evenings and transfers. Safety for tourists is generally good across Vietnam’s main stay areas when you use normal big-city awareness: keep phones secure on busy sidewalks, use reputable ride apps, and follow hotel advice on local quirks. Food is one of the joys of basing yourself well. Explore a few streets beyond the first tourist row, follow busy local counters, and balance street meals with one or two sit-down dinners so your trip has both energy and comfort. Ultimately the right cluster is the one that matches how you want to wake up, move and wind down. Use the map and filters above to compare walkability, quietness and access, then browse stays in this neighbourhood with that rhythm in mind.",
